WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.450 --> 00:00:03.600
Taking your breaks is part of the job.

2
00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:06.655
It protects your well-being, and it protects your pay.

3
00:00:08.005 --> 00:00:10.628
Rest breaks are 10 minutes, and they are paid.

4
00:00:10.628 --> 00:00:12.737
You get one in every 4 hours of work.

5
00:00:12.737 --> 00:00:17.755
They are already counted in your hours worked, so you never enter them on your timecard.

6
00:00:19.105 --> 00:00:20.628
Meal breaks are unpaid.

7
00:00:20.628 --> 00:00:24.895
Unpaid meal breaks are determined by the applicable work location state.

8
00:00:24.895 --> 00:00:31.253
Once you have worked 5 hours, you must be given 30 minutes or more, completely relieved of duty.

9
00:00:31.253 --> 00:00:34.764
After 10 hours, a second 30-minute meal break is due.

10
00:00:36.114 --> 00:00:37.537
Two things you cannot do.

11
00:00:37.537 --> 00:00:43.858
You cannot skip your meal break and stop working 30 minutes early, and you cannot bank break time to use later.

12
00:00:45.208 --> 00:00:52.255
If you were involuntarily prevented from taking a meal break, enter your hours as one continuous block, with no gap.

13
00:00:52.255 --> 00:00:56.386
Workday then generates the meal break payment in your next paycheck.

14
00:00:57.736 --> 00:01:03.347
For a missed rest break, tell your leader using the Notice of Involuntarily Missed Rest Break form.
